<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept motorbike exports fall 8.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept motorbike exports fall 8.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's motorcycle exports fell</p>
<p>8.4 percent from a year earlier to 116,348 in September, the</p>
<p>Japan Automobile Manufacturers Association (JAMA) said on</p>
<p>Tuesday.</p>
<p>Motorcycle exports in September by Japan's four makers</p>
<p>(with percentage change from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Honda Motor	44,673  up    5.1 percent</p>
<p> Yamaha Motor     29,861  down 31.5 percent</p>
<p> Suzuki Motor     22,347  down  6.5 percent</p>
<p> Kawasaki Heavy   19,467  up   14.4 percent</p>
<p>Japan's motorcycle exports in April-September fell 10</p>
<p>percent from a year earlier to 640,137 units.</p>
<p>Exports in April-September by the four makers:</p>
<p> Honda Motor		  262,129  up   22.9 percent</p>
<p> Yamaha Motor		 160,208  up    1.0 percent</p>
<p> Suzuki Motor		 142,217  down 15.8 percent</p>
<p> Kawasaki Heavy		75,583  down  8.9 percent</p>
